  "notes": "Governmental funds cash basis; business-type activities accrual basis (Statement of Net Position and Statement of Activities print business-type on accrual), so business_type measure is net position from the proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Fund Net Position (p7), as in FY2023; business-type disbursements total 671,999 printed on the Statement of Activities (p2) = operating expenses 620,446 + interest 45,253 + debt issuance costs 6,300; receipts total computed. Proprietary cash flows from p8 Totals column. Governmental: fund balance 864,949 + 2,055,601 - 1,969,859 + loan proceeds 50,000 + transfers 150,000 = 1,150,691. Beginning cash not printed (only cash basis fund balance), left null; ending cash = the printed cash lines on p4. Business: 3,377,802 + 1,072,083 - 671,999 - 150,000 = 3,627,886. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement (p4, total 1,150,691 equals the government-wide governmental column p1); business-type lines from the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1); 'Due in More Than One Year' 2,926,101 includes meter deposits 11,465 (p6). Grants 183,683: grantor not printed, so category other / detail Grants (user ruling 2026-11-12; FY2023 had state aid). Airport Authority component unit excluded. Detail: General, Water and Sewer budgetary comparison schedules (pp9-11; Water/Sewer schedules are cash basis while the proprietary statement is accrual); Water/Sewer printed totals are operating only, so non-operating lines and transfers are outside_printed_total. Water 'Bond Issuance Costs' budget printed as 2,395,000 (inflow sign) left out of budget_final. No schedule for the nonmajor Debt Service fund. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
}
